# magic(5) pattern for SCF documents.
#
# An .scf is a SQLite 3 database (spec §1.1), so file(1) reports it as
# one by default. The application_id at header offset 68 is what makes
# it identifiable as SCF specifically — see spec §1.2 and
# scf-core/src/fileIdentity.ts.
#
# Install locally:
#     mkdir -p ~/.magic.d && cp spec/scf.magic ~/.magic.d/scf
#     file --magic-file ~/.magic.d/scf yourfile.scf
#
# The stanza below follows the form used by sqlite/magic.txt, which is
# where it should eventually be upstreamed so that a stock file(1)
# recognises SCF without configuration.

0	string	=SQLite\ format\ 3
>68	belong	=0x53434631	Story Context Framework document
>>60	belong	>0		\b, schema
>>>60	belong/1000	x	\b %d
>>>60	belong%1000	x	\b.%d
